-- 035: units for the foods people count, from USDA FoodData Central, and the
-- last staples (version 18: UNIT-10, UNIT-13, UNIT-14, FOOD-10, FOOD-11).
--
--  1. Units on the shared foods bought or used by the piece: a cauliflower
--     and its florets, a head and a leaf of lettuce, a stalk of celery, a
--     sprig of parsley, a tin of chickpeas. The weights are USDA's measured
--     portion weights (SR Legacy, April 2018: public domain), each unit marked
--     "USDA FoodData Central". A unit's weight is what is eaten; a whole piece
--     also says what it weighs as bought, from USDA's refuse share (peel,
--     core, stone). They are additions to NEVO's foods, keyed by NEVO's code:
--     no NEVO value changes. RIVM Portie-online's units stay and win where
--     both give a piece.
--  2. The extra-large egg (EU grade XL, 73 g and over in the shell): 68.6 g
--     eaten, worked out from the EU grade and USDA's shell share (see
--     scripts/units-usda.mjs, EGG_XL).
--  3. Staples the catalogue lacked: a plain bagel, a chicken thigh fillet and
--     a chicken thigh with skin, as shared foods from USDA, marked with source
--     and version. NEVO's crunchy muesli is shown as granola, its chicken
--     fillet as chicken breast fillet (display names are GetIt's additions;
--     NEVO's own names stay beside them).
--  4. NEVO's "Human milk" (code 297) is hidden from the shared list, as the
--     old catalogue's was (027). Hiding is not an amendment: the row stays.
--
-- Generated by scripts/units-usda.mjs. A shared food's units and name only
-- change here, so the whole list is written; a row is only touched when
-- something in it changes, so every device's next sync brings exactly the
-- foods that changed. Safe to run more than once.

